# Credit Risk Classification

## Project Overview
Machine learning project to predict credit risk using the German Credit Dataset.

## Dataset
- Source: German Credit Data (Kaggle)
- 1,000 clients, 10 features
- Target: Risk (good/bad) — evaluated by credit specialists

## Tools Used
- Python
- pandas, numpy, matplotlib
- scikit-learn (Logistic Regression)

## Results
- Accuracy: 75.5%
- Good Risk Recall: 91%
- Bad Risk Recall: 37%

## Key Insights
- Clients with higher credit amounts tend to be higher risk
- Younger clients (20-30) represent the highest volume of bad risk
- Dataset is imbalanced: 70% good, 30% bad

## Next Steps
- Apply SMOTE to balance the dataset
- Test Random Forest or XGBoost
- Tune decision threshold to improve bad risk detection
